{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1276571-making-your-own-chimerical-army-city","id":1276571,"title":"Making your own Chimerical Army/City!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-24T23:29:14-08:00","id":1276571,"title":"Making your own Chimerical Army/City!","content":"Hohohoho merry Christmas! Thinking about the North Pole and how it could have a Changeling City hidden in the Artic wastes gives me some ideas...<br /> <br /> So while Changeling Numbers are rather limited, they are still large enough to create courts second in size only to Wraiths.<br /> <br /> But how would a county of what 40 Changelings compare to a Castle of say 5 Changelings and 200+ Chimera!?<br /> <br /> So mostly the books just keep Chimera as the occasional wildlife, or pets of Changelings. But nothing stops a Changeling from having a chimerical retinue? And with players guide popping out rules now\u2019s as good a time as any to discuss what about say a lone Sidhe lord, or even a Commoner with dreams of Nobility, using their own personal magical Potence to either Create or tame a large population of Chimera? If they are at least as smart as toddlers you can have them swear oaths of Fealty, train them, cloth them and basically be a full blown king out in the middle of the woods, or a sheikh in a hidden oasis, or Hell Santa himself out in the North Pole!<br /> <br /> This feels like a nice way to really shore up Fae lords by giving them a city of Fae citizens! Master Crafters can craft their own chimerical Automata, witches can birth talking beasts of the wild, and woodsmen can tame those who dwell hidden. While one lone potent Fae could certainly do this, this could really shine when it\u2019s a circle.<br /> <br /> This is rich with potential as you could have an individual separated from the known power structure and politics, someone who seemed to come out of nowhere but is singly mighty enough to challenge a Duke!<br /> <br /> Like say you hade an old Greybeard dedicate his life to building a Freehold and so he winds up erecting one in secret in the wilderness and before he dies he unleashes enough to create and bind a basic staff of guardians and caretakers tasked to keep it in good condition till there greybeard reincarnates. The greybeard reincarnates and develops as a secret lord in this hidden redoubt and learns to create reliable Chimera and oath them to service. He then gets a Changeling Motley around him to help, now boom they cultivate a few hundred citizens under a Mountain or lake. They might even bring enchanted mortals or kinain.<br /> <br /> <br /> And what if you do this with the already established power structure? Maybe each of King David\u2019s Freeholds ( I think he keeps three) has hundreds of hobgoblins, and dozens of enchanted mortals and kinain, and a couple dozen Changelings.<br /> <br /> This also seems fitting for Inanimae or Merfolk!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T16:00:16-08:00","id":1276699,"title":"","content":"I am thinking a good idea for a Scenario is to have one of these chimerical nations at the North Pole, with Knockers and Boggans as as the crafter generals and the Christmas elves as the work army, and reindeer pooka and a beefy Polar bear pooka as the warden of security. Maybe Mrs. Clause is a house Liam Sidhe and Santa was lost in the late fifties or 60s, and eventually his mortal body died.<br /> <br /> Santa would be the rare House Aesin Sidhe who stayed in the Autumn world and became an Autumn Sidhe. He is also in my headcanon the Ghost of Odin so his throne is Highshelf which allows him to see across the globe and he possesses Gungnir, which looks like a simple shepherds crook to mortals. When he is reborn his Sidhe self will go for a mortal to reincarnate in and Gungnir will find a mortal to make a Chosen, a Kith I designed that like selkie are Fae bound to an item, in this case instead of a shirt of seal the Chosen are the panoply of the gods.<br /> <br /> And the players could be the motley of Santa\u2019s new reincarnation or they are trying to find him.<br /> <br /> And you can choose if you want Santa to be old or a young bishounen Santa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T01:51:09-08:00","id":1276764,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d have the Knockers be the crafter generals and Boggans as workshop elves, the reindeer Pooka is a fine idea while I\u2019d have the old man himself be a Satyr. So santa would be much more like his original incarnation, so not necessarily that jolly or nice even, while Krampus would be either an Unseelie Satyr or even a Nasty. <br /> The elven spies who gather knowledge so they can make their judgement would be Chimeras in my mind.<br /> <br /> Both would be equally likely to punish the wicked children as to gift the nice ones, note that both would judge matters much more stricktly than modern people are used to.<br /> <br /> Though my santa doesn\u2019t live in the north pole...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T02:16:45-08:00","id":1276765,"title":"","content":"Where does he live? Detroit?<br /> <br /> Well I was just thinking Boggans can arguably be as good a crafter as a Knocker and just the general idea that all the Changelings are higher up then Chimera.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Krampus the book illustrates one as an Example Lurker, but yeah it works to have him possible a Satyr or Nasty.<br /> <br /> Maybe that Old Wyld Hunt Phallic proto-Santa is the last incarnation of the Krampus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T02:29:45-08:00","id":1276769,"title":"","content":"Great ideas! One could easily make a whole campaign of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T05:30:38-08:00","id":1276773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1276571-making-your-own-chimerical-army-city?p=1276765#post1276765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does he live? Detroit?</div> </div> </div> </div>A place called Korvatunturi or \u201dEar Fell\u201d in English. (Though Detroit makes me grin like a maniac.)<br /> <br /> As for Boggans while they are excellent craftsmen they just fit perfectly into my vision of worker elves building a ridiculous amounts of stuff together while Knockers seem more fitting for management and innovation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T12:28:20-08:00","id":1276846,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s true but one of the issues with Knocker is they are perfectionists that can\u2019t reach perfection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}